Background VU1 compiler (GOW_VU1N_JIT, experimental): VU1 blocks the game reaches without native code are compiled while
it runs, with the build's own generator and compiler, and switch to native code a few seconds later.
- ps2_vu1_jit.inl (new): a slot set up without native code queues its 16 KB micro memory (once per code generation); a
  worker thread at low priority writes the images, runs tools/vu1/vu1n_gen.py --dll (blocks the game already has left
  out), compiles the module (clang, the build's flags: GOW_VU1N_JIT_CXX / _PY / _GEN / _FLAGS) as a DLL / shared object
  and loads it; runNative registers its blocks at the next entry and sets the dispatch slots up again. Modules are kept
  in <GOW_VU1N_JIT>/<stamp> (generator + ABI + compiler command) and loaded at the next start. Processes run hidden
  (CREATE_NO_WINDOW) below normal priority.
- ps2_vu1_native.h: VU1JitApi, the table through which a module reaches the VU1NativeAccess functions that are not
  inline here (chain, callLower, callUpper, xgkick) and registers its blocks; kVu1JitAbi (sizes of what the blocks touch)
  makes a module of other headers register nothing. NativeState: jitSeen / jitQueuedAt.
- vu1n_gen.py: --dll <name> writes one module (VU1NativeAccess thunks + exported vu1n_jit_blocks()) and <name>.keys;
  --skip-keys leaves out known blocks. Without them the output is unchanged.
- tests/vu1_jit_test.cpp + tools/ci/pruebas_vu1.cmake: a procedural micro memory (transform loop with LQI, MULA/MADDA/
  MADD, CLIP, DIV/WAITQ, MULq, FCGET, FMAND, SQI, IBNE; an FMAC/flag mix) run in the exact engine and through the
  background compiler. Checked on Linux (clang 18): 4000 random cases, the module's results have the same digest as the
  same blocks compiled into the executable (bit-identical; both differ from the exact engine in the same 284 edge cases
  with Inf/NaN/denormal inputs, the native backend's known DIV rounding); transform loop 17.4 us exact engine, 0.89 us
  background-compiled, 0.82 us compiled in; one micro memory compiled in ~1.5 s.
Off unless GOW_VU1N_JIT is set (the launcher sets it for clang builds when "Compile new areas while playing" is on).

